quick-question packaging
========================

The Debian packaging lives on the `debian` branch of the upstream repository.

  main     platform-agnostic upstream source; never contains debian/
  debian   main plus debian/ and .github/workflows/release-deb.yml

The source format is 3.0 (quilt). The packaging does not modify upstream
files: everything Debian-specific is under debian/, plus the GitHub workflow,
which dpkg-source ignores through debian/source/options. There are no quilt
patches. If upstream needs a change, make it on main and merge it here.


Updating to a new upstream version
----------------------------------

    git checkout debian
    git merge main
    # add a debian/changelog entry for <upstream-version>-1, e.g. with
    dch -v 0.3.0-1 "New upstream release."

The upstream part of the version must match QQ_VERSION in src/qq.h; the
GitHub workflow checks this. For a packaging-only change, bump the Debian
revision instead (0.2.0-2).

The changelog distribution is an Ubuntu series (currently "resolute"),
because lintian on Ubuntu rejects Debian's "unstable".


Building
--------

Binary packages only (this is what the GitHub workflow does):

    sudo apt install debhelper lintian libcurl4-openssl-dev libcjson-dev python3
    dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b
    lintian ../quick-question_0.2.0-1_amd64.deb
    sudo apt install ../quick-question_0.2.0-1_amd64.deb

The build runs the upstream test suite. Set DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS=nocheck to
skip it. The package installs /usr/bin/qq, the qq(1) man page, README.md, and
config.example.json under /usr/share/doc/quick-question/examples/.

A source package also needs the orig tarball. Create it from the upstream
commit this branch last merged:

    git archive --format=tar.gz --prefix=quick-question-0.2.0/ \
        -o ../quick-question_0.2.0.orig.tar.gz "$(git merge-base HEAD main)"
    dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc


GitHub Actions
--------------

.github/workflows/release-deb.yml runs on every push to the debian branch.
It:

  1. checks that the upstream part of the debian/changelog version matches
     QQ_VERSION;
  2. builds on ubuntu-24.04, running the tests;
  3. runs lintian;
  4. publishes a GitHub release tagged debian/<version> on the pushed commit,
     with quick-question_<version>_amd64.deb attached and the changelog entry
     as its notes.

There is one release per package version. A push that doesn't change the
debian/changelog version still builds and lints, but leaves the existing
release alone and logs a notice. To publish a new package, add a changelog
entry (a new upstream version or a new Debian revision) and push.
